  <div id="sutta">
  
              <h2 id="SN1.69" class="h1">Desire<br/>
                Icchā Sutta  (SN 1:69)</h2>
              <div class="verse">
                <p>“With what         is the world tied down?</p>
                <p class="v1">With the subduing</p>
                <p>of what         is it freed?</p>
                <p class="v1">With the abandoning</p>
                <p>of what</p>
                <p class="v5">are all bonds</p>
                <p class="v5">cut through?”</p>
                <div class="verse-add">
                  <p class="vspk">The Buddha:</p>
                  <p>“With desire         the world is tied down.</p>
                  <p>With the subduing</p>
                  <p>of desire         it’s freed.</p>
                  <p>With the abandoning</p>
                  <p>of desire</p>
                  <p class="v5">all bonds</p>
                  <p class="v5">are cut through.”</p>
                </div>
              </div>
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
